  "summary": "NEXTDC plans an AI factory and technology campus, called M4, on the former Westgate Park printing complex at 127 Todd Road in Port Melbourne's Fishermans Bend precinct. Announced in June 2025 as an A$2 billion project of up to 150 MW, designed for very high-density Nvidia-class AI racks and linked with university, defence and research partners, it received development approval from the Victorian Government by January 2026, when NEXTDC cited 162 MW. Construction timing has not been published.",
